WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:05.070
Three lines of Java. Waits, screenshots
and a report included.

00:00:06.317 --> 00:00:12.092
In plain Selenium, the same test needs an
explicit wait, a screenshot helper,

00:00:12.092 --> 00:00:15.917
report wiring, and a separate client for
API calls.

00:00:16.217 --> 00:00:19.677
Every team writes that plumbing, and every
copy drifts.

00:00:19.977 --> 00:00:25.100
Measured on the same test, that is 44
lines in plain Selenium,

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.587
and 17 with SHAFT.

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.640
SHAFT puts every surface behind one entry
point.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:37.911
SHAFT.GUI.WebDriver drives browsers and
Appium

00:00:37.911 --> 00:00:41.694
apps. SHAFT.API wraps REST Assured.

00:00:41.694 --> 00:00:47.422
SHAFT.DB and SHAFT.CLI cover databases and
terminals.

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:52.389
Test data comes from JSON, Excel, CSV or
YAML files,

00:00:52.389 --> 00:00:56.510
and every check uses the same assertThat
style.

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:01.310
SHAFT handles timing for you.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:05.595
Every element action retries until the
element is ready,

00:01:05.595 --> 00:01:07.730
up to a timeout you configure.

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:11.997
After navigation, it waits for the page to
go quiet:

00:01:11.997 --> 00:01:15.430
300 milliseconds without changes, by
default.

00:01:15.730 --> 00:01:19.373
For business states, like an order status
turning complete,

00:01:19.373 --> 00:01:21.720
you wait on that condition explicitly.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.322
Retries are opt-in and bounded,

00:01:24.322 --> 00:01:28.630
and locators can target accessible roles
and visible text.

00:01:31.583 --> 00:01:36.576
Every action becomes an Allure step.
Failures get screenshots by default,

00:01:36.576 --> 00:01:39.243
and validation points can get them too.

00:01:39.543 --> 00:01:40.822
When a test fails,

00:01:40.822 --> 00:01:45.158
SHAFT attaches a diagnostics bundle and a
trace with the DOM,

00:01:45.158 --> 00:01:48.143
network and console evidence it collected.

00:01:48.443 --> 00:01:52.223
So the report explains the failure, not
just the stack trace.

00:01:55.183 --> 00:01:58.293
Where tests run is configuration, not
code.

00:01:58.593 --> 00:02:03.927
Change the execution address, and the same
class runs locally, in Docker,

00:02:03.927 --> 00:02:07.873
on a Selenium Grid, or on BrowserStack and
LambdaTest.

00:02:08.173 --> 00:02:11.740
Cross browser mode can run one class on
Chrome,

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:15.003
Firefox and Safari in parallel with
Docker.

00:02:15.303 --> 00:02:17.535
Use TestNG, JUnit or Cucumber,

00:02:17.535 --> 00:02:20.809
and switch the browser backend to
Playwright

00:02:20.809 --> 00:02:23.413
without rewriting your SHAFT steps.

00:02:26.350 --> 00:02:29.610
Already have a Selenium suite? Run the
upgrader.

00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:34.914
It compiles your project first, adds the
SHAFT bill of materials and engine,

00:02:34.914 --> 00:02:37.680
and keeps your existing tests as they are.

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:43.160
If the build fails afterwards, every
touched file is restored, byte for byte.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:44.788
When you are ready,

00:02:44.788 --> 00:02:50.240
session and full modes rewrite Selenium
code inside the same safe transaction.

00:02:51.183 --> 00:02:55.833
The agentic tools are optional, and they
work without an AI provider.

00:02:56.133 --> 00:03:00.716
Capture records a flow and generates
compiling test code.

00:03:00.716 --> 00:03:03.690
Doctor diagnoses failed runs offline.

00:03:03.690 --> 00:03:08.273
Heal recovers changed locators and
explains every choice.

00:03:08.573 --> 00:03:14.123
The same tools reach IntelliJ through a
plugin, and any agent through MCP.

00:03:17.083 --> 00:03:20.497
SHAFT is MIT licensed and built in

00:03:20.497 --> 00:03:24.213
public since 2018, with 216 releases.

00:03:24.613 --> 00:03:28.986
Generate a project at shafthq.github.io,
run mvn

00:03:28.986 --> 00:03:31.992
